// DGA-owned native menu fields. Limits match readSettings(); no native profile IDs.
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Enabled","Dynamic Attendance","Let fans arrive late, leave early and take halftime breaks as the game unfolds.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"Profile","Fan Patience","Automatic chooses patience from the matchup and weather. Normal uses standard departures; Patient Fans slows departures; Bad Weather makes fans leave sooner.",0,0,3,Kind::Profile},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"ArrivalsEnabled","Fans Arriving After Kickoff","Start with some fans still outside and let them arrive during the first quarter, up to the crowd originally supplied by the game.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"StartPercent","Starting Crowd (%)","Starting attendance for most schools, as a share of the game's original crowd. Higher means more fans at kickoff; lower means more empty seats. Matchup and weather can adjust it.",55.0,30.0,90.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateSchoolStartPercent","Late-Arriving Schools: Start (%)","Starting attendance for UCLA, Miami (FL), Georgia Tech and Maryland. Higher means more fans at kickoff; lower means more arrive later. Matchup and weather can adjust it.",40.0,30.0,80.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"FinishPercentOfQuarter","Arrivals Finish: Through Q1 (%)","How far through the first quarter most schools finish filling in. Higher means later arrivals; lower means the crowd fills sooner. 25 means one quarter of Q1 has elapsed.",25.0,10.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateSchoolFinishPercentOfQuarter","Late Schools: Arrivals Finish (%)","How far through Q1 UCLA, Miami (FL), Georgia Tech and Maryland finish filling in. Higher means later arrivals; lower means they fill sooner. 75 means three quarters of Q1 have elapsed.",75.0,10.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"HalftimeSeatBreakStrength","Fans Away at Halftime (%)","How many fans temporarily leave their seats around halftime. Higher means more empty seats; lower means fewer. 100 is normal strength; 0 turns this off. Fans who stay return early in Q3.",100.0,0.0,200.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"HalftimeDepartureConversionPercent","Halftime Fans Who Stay Away (%)","How many fans on a halftime break may leave for good during a home blowout. Higher means more stay away; lower means more return. 0 turns this off. Applies to ordinary home games.",25.0,0.0,25.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"BigGameBonus","Rivalry Starting Crowd Bonus","Extra starting attendance for rivalry games, in percentage points. Higher means more fans at kickoff; lower means a smaller rivalry bonus. The final crowd cannot exceed the original attendance.",10.0,0.0,10.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"BigGameStartPercent","Big Game Starting Crowd (%)","Starting attendance for games between two Top 25 teams and for postseason games. Higher means more fans at kickoff; lower means more arrive later. Starting attendance stays at least 60%.",60.0,60.0,90.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"BadWeatherPenalty","Bad Weather Crowd Reduction","Starting-attendance reduction for rain or snow, in percentage points. Higher means fewer fans at kickoff; lower means a smaller weather penalty. 0 removes this penalty.",10.0,0.0,10.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"FcsOpponentPenalty","FCS Opponent Crowd Reduction","Starting-attendance reduction when facing an FCS team, in percentage points. Higher means fewer fans at kickoff; lower means a smaller FCS penalty. 0 removes this penalty.",10.0,0.0,10.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"ComebackOriginalDeficit","Comeback: Earlier Deficit (Points)","How far the home team must have fallen behind before a comeback can slow fan departures. Higher requires a larger earlier deficit; lower lets smaller comebacks qualify. 21 means a three-touchdown deficit.",21.0,14.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"ComebackPointsRecovered","Comeback: Points Made Up","How much of an earlier deficit the home team must erase to slow fan departures. Higher requires more points made up; lower starts protecting the crowd sooner.",14.0,7.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"ComebackDeteriorationSeconds","Comeback Patience (Seconds)","How long fans give a fading comeback before its departure protection ends. Higher keeps fans patient longer; lower ends protection sooner. Uses game-clock seconds, scaled from 12-minute quarters.",60.0,0.0,600.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"TwoMinuteWarning","Check Departures at Two Minutes","Recheck whether fans should leave at the next safe break after the fourth-quarter clock reaches 2:00.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"MaximumDeparturePerQuarter","Fans Leaving per Quarter (%)","Normal limit on fans leaving permanently in one quarter, as a share of the original crowd. Higher allows more to leave; lower keeps more fans. Postseason limits and the late-blowout allowance still apply.",45.0,1.0,50.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"MaximumDeparturePerTransition","Crowd Change per Break (%)","Base crowd change allowed during each play-selection screen or other safe break. Higher makes seats empty or refill faster; lower makes each change smaller. Longer waits can allow larger changes.",4.0,1.0,20.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateTrafficEnabled","Beat the Traffic Departures","Let fans leave faster in the final 25% of Q4 when the home team has little chance of coming back. This starts in the last three minutes with 12-minute quarters.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateTrafficExtraQuarterAllowance","Late Blowout: Extra Departures (%)","Extra share of the original crowd allowed to leave beyond the Q4 limit during a 28+ point home blowout. Higher allows more departures; lower keeps more fans. 0 removes this extra allowance.",10.0,0.0,10.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateTurnoverExtraMax","Late Turnover: Extra Departures (%)","Maximum extra share of the original crowd that may leave after a costly late home turnover. Higher allows a larger exodus; lower limits it. 0 turns this off. A turnover must seriously hurt the comeback chance.",10.0,0.0,15.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"FormulaStrength","Fans Leaving Early (%)","Overall strength of departures caused by the score, time and matchup. Higher makes more fans leave; lower keeps more fans. 100 is normal; 0 turns off these departures. Halftime and late-score departures have separate controls.",100.0,0.0,200.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Attendance",L"Dynamic Gameday Attendance",L"LateScoreExtra","Late Opponent Score: Departures (%)","Extra share of the original crowd that may leave after an opponent score in the final two minutes, with home down 9+ and at most one timeout. Higher means more leave; lower means fewer. 0 turns this off; home regular-season games only.",5.0,0.0,25.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"Enabled","Crowd Sound Effects","Adjust crowd excitement to the occupied seats and enable added crowd sounds. Turning this on after starting the game with it off requires a game restart.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"NativeQuietingStrengthPercent","Small Crowd Excitement Reduction (%)","How much calmer the game's crowd becomes when many seats are empty. Higher reduces excitement more; lower keeps more of the game's original excitement. 0 turns this off. Changes fade in gradually.",100.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"CrowdVolumeReductionPercent","Small Stadium Volume Reduction (%)","Maximum extra volume reduction for small stadiums with sparse crowds. Higher makes them quieter; lower keeps them louder. 0 removes this reduction. Larger stadiums use the excitement reduction instead.",25.0,0.0,25.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"ReductionStartPercent","Quiet Crowd Below Fullness (%)","Stadium fullness below which the crowd begins to calm down. Higher starts quieting while more seats are occupied; lower waits until the stands are emptier. The change grows as more fans leave.",50.0,1.0,50.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"LayeredAtmosphereEnabled","Added Crowd Atmosphere","Add crowd roars, cheers, excitement, volume boosts and camera reactions when the game situation and stadium fullness qualify.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"OpeningAtmosphere","Opening Game Atmosphere","Add crowd buildup during the stadium introduction and early first quarter. Big games can qualify from 50% fullness before the normal requirement gradually returns.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"OvertimeAtmosphere","Overtime Crowd Atmosphere","Keep added crowd energy going between snaps during qualifying overtime situations. Stadium fullness requirements still apply.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"PlayCallAtmosphere","Play Selection Atmosphere","Add crowd roars and rising anticipation during play selection, plus ordinary successful-play reactions. Special cheers are for the home offense; the away offense gets roars and swells.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"UpsetWatchAtmosphere","Upset Watch Crowd Sounds","Build crowd excitement from Q2 onward when a home underdog threatens a Top 25 visitor. Needs at least 50% stadium fullness. At neutral sites, either underdog can qualify.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"SkillMoveReactions","Skill Move and Big Hit Reactions","Add a short swell and gentle shake buildup for skill moves and broken tackles. Trucks use the native big-hit crowd sound; hit sticks keep an impact. Touchdowns and major celebrations take priority.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"StaggeredMajorCheers","Second Cheer for Major Plays","Allow one delayed follow-up cheer after a major play or celebration. Includes cheers already playing and keeps the existing volume limits.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"PackedBigGameReactions","Bigger Reactions in Packed Big Games","Make important moments stronger in packed ranked games, championships and rivalries. Confirmed game-saving stops can trigger the biggest celebration; a first down that seals the win can feel like a touchdown.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"DuringPlayReactionsEnabled","Live Play Crowd Reactions","Add crowd and camera reactions to qualifying long gains, interceptions, fumbles, sacks, third/fourth-down defensive catch knockouts and returns. The stadium must meet the fullness requirement for that situation.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"LongCompletionMinimumYards","Long Catch Reaction: Yards","Gain needed at the catch to trigger a long-pass reaction. Higher requires a deeper catch; lower reacts to shorter catches. A short catch can still qualify later through yards after the catch.",20.0,10.0,60.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"LongGainMinimumYards","Long Run or Catch-and-Run: Yards","Total gain needed for a run or catch-and-run reaction. Higher waits for a longer gain; lower reacts sooner. Camera shake builds over the five yards before this mark.",15.0,10.0,60.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"PassFlightAnticipation","Crowd Swell During Passes","Let the crowd build anticipation while a qualifying pass is in the air, then settle after the catch or incompletion. Requires Live Play Crowd Reactions.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"SituationalCrowdReactions","Crowd Cheers and Disappointment","Add disappointment for costly home mistakes and deep visitor catches, plus cheers for defensive pass breakups and tackles for loss.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"ChantMaximumBoostPercent","Chant Volume Boost Limit (%)","Maximum extra chant volume at full attendance. Higher allows louder chants; lower keeps them closer to normal. 0 removes the boost. The boost grows above 75% stadium fullness.",15.0,0.0,15.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"BigGameMinimumFullnessPercent","Big Game Fullness Requirement (%)","Extra minimum fullness for big-game buildup, critical downs and goal-line tension. Higher requires fuller stands; lower allows emptier stands, subject to the existing stadium-size requirement.",55.0,55.0,90.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"WinningEruptions","Major Celebrations","Use the biggest crowd celebration for special plays: the first touchdown in the opening two plays, decisive late scores, overtime winners and game-sealing takeaways. Long touchdowns in close games get a modest touchdown boost instead.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"PackedHouseBuildup","Packed Stadium Atmosphere","Allow play-selection buildup in ordinary matchups when enough seats are filled. Smaller stadiums need a higher fullness percentage than larger stadiums.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"DriveEscalation","Build Excitement During Drives","Let successful drives build crowd excitement. Stalled drives cool the crowd; scores and possession changes reset the buildup.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"MaximumBoostPercent","Normal Crowd Volume Boost Limit (%)","Maximum extra crowd volume during ordinary atmosphere. Higher allows a louder crowd; lower limits the boost. 0 also turns off added atmosphere. The boost grows above 75% fullness.",25.0,0.0,25.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"HighLeverageBoostPercent","Critical Moment Volume Boost (%)","Total extra crowd volume allowed in close critical situations. Higher allows louder moments; lower limits them, without going below normal crowd volume. This replaces the normal boost rather than adding to it.",35.0,0.0,35.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Crowd Sound",L"Dynamic Gameday Soundscape",L"EruptionBoostPercent","Major Celebration Volume Boost (%)","Total extra crowd volume allowed during the biggest celebrations. Higher allows louder celebrations; lower limits them. 0 keeps normal crowd volume. This replaces the normal boost rather than adding to it.",50.0,0.0,50.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"ExtraReplaysEnabled","Additional Replays","Allow the mod to request extra replays after plays. The game can still show its own replays when this is off.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"PauseMenuFullness","Show Fullness in Pause Menu","Show Stadium Fullness beside Resume in the pause menu. This is the share of seats filled, updated when the menu opens. A dash means the measurement is not ready.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"InsetAfterRoutinePlays","Small Replays After Routine Plays","Allow small replay windows during play selection after ordinary runs and completions.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"FullScreenBigPlays","Full-Screen Big Play Replays","Encourage full-screen replays for big plays. The game's usual skip controls still work.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"DefensiveHighlights","Defensive Play Replays","Allow extra replay opportunities after sacks and tackles for loss, while keeping interception and lost-fumble highlights.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"FullScreenMinimumYards","Full-Screen Replay: Minimum Yards","Gain needed for an added full-screen big-play replay opportunity. Higher favors longer plays; lower lets shorter plays qualify. The game still decides whether to show the replay.",15.0,10.0,60.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"CameraShake","Added Camera Shake","Enable all camera shake added by the mod. The game's Dynamic Camera Effects setting must also be On.",1.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"NativeShakeMinimumFullnessPercent","Stadium Pulse: Minimum Fullness (%)","Minimum filled-seat percentage for the game's own Stadium Pulse shake. Higher blocks it in more empty stadiums; lower allows it with fewer fans. 0 removes this filter. The Pulse meter and gameplay advantage are unchanged.",50.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"OrdinaryShakeStrengthPercent","Normal Play Selection Shake (%)","Maximum added shake during ordinary play selection. Higher gives stronger movement; lower gives gentler movement. 0 turns this type off. Camera zoom is accounted for.",5.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"CriticalShakeStrengthPercent","Critical Down Shake (%)","Maximum added shake before qualifying third and fourth downs in close games. Higher makes it stronger; lower makes it gentler. 0 turns this type off. Fullness requirements still apply.",10.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"PlayReactionFadeSeconds","After-Play Reaction Fade (Seconds)","How long ordinary live-play reactions settle after the whistle, including a short hold and fade. Higher lets them linger longer; lower ends them sooner. Touchdowns and major celebrations use separate durations.",5.0,1.0,8.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"PlayImpactExtraSeconds","Short Impact Extra Time (Seconds)","Extra time for reactions to sacks, similar defensive impacts and long catches stopped immediately. Higher makes these reactions last longer; lower shortens them. 0 adds no extra time.",1.0,0.0,5.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"CatchImpactShakeStrengthPercent","Stopped Long Catch Shake (%)","Shake strength when a long catch ends immediately in a tackle or whistle. Higher makes the impact stronger; lower makes it gentler. 0 turns this type off. Catches followed by a run use Live Play Shake.",8.0,0.0,30.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"LineupCheerShakeStrengthPercent","Special Play Selection Shake (%)","Shake accompanying a special home-offense cheer, such as inside the 10-yard line or the first offensive play selection. Higher makes it stronger; lower makes it gentler. 0 turns this type off.",5.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"HostileOpeningShakeMaximumPercent","First Away Possession Shake (%)","Maximum extra shake on the game's first offensive play when the visitors start with the ball. Higher makes it stronger; lower makes it gentler. 0 turns this type off. Requires Opening Game Atmosphere.",15.0,0.0,30.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"TouchdownShakeStrengthPercent","Touchdown Shake: Sustained (%)","Shake strength after the opening touchdown impact. Higher makes the sustained celebration stronger; lower makes it gentler. 0 turns off touchdown shake. Major celebrations use their own settings.",15.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"EruptionShakeStrengthPercent","Major Celebration: Sustained (%)","Shake strength after the opening impact of the biggest celebrations. Higher makes the sustained shake stronger; lower makes it gentler. 0 turns off this celebration shake.",22.5,0.0,100.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"TouchdownShakeImpactPercent","Touchdown Shake: Opening Hit (%)","Strength of the initial touchdown shake before it settles. Higher gives a stronger opening hit; lower softens it, but never below the sustained strength. The sustained setting must be above 0.",20.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"EruptionShakeImpactPercent","Major Celebration: Opening Hit (%)","Strength of the initial shake for the biggest celebrations. Higher gives a stronger opening hit; lower softens it, but never below the sustained strength. The sustained setting must be above 0.",30.0,0.0,100.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"TouchdownShakeDurationSeconds","Touchdown Shake Duration (Seconds)","Total touchdown shake time, including the opening hit, hold and fade. Higher makes it last longer; lower ends it sooner. Safeties use 70% of this duration. This changes camera shake, not celebration sound.",11.0,3.0,30.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"EruptionShakeDurationSeconds","Major Shake Duration (Seconds)","Total shake time for the biggest celebrations, including the opening hit, hold and fade. Higher makes it last longer; lower ends it sooner. This changes camera shake, not celebration sound.",16.0,5.0,60.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"DuringPlayShakeStrengthPercent","Live Play Shake (%)","Shake for long gains, interceptions, sacks and forced fumbles. Higher makes it stronger; lower makes it gentler. 0 turns it off. Kick/punt returns build from 30 yards to this strength at 40. Fumble pickups add no shake.",10.0,0.0,30.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Camera and Replays",L"Dynamic Gameday Broadcast",L"CannonShakeStrengthPercent","Stadium Cannon Shake (%)","Shake when a stadium cannon fires, independent of Live Play Shake. Higher makes the blast stronger; lower makes it gentler. 0 turns cannon shake off without changing its sound. Works at any crowd fullness and respects Dynamic Camera Effects.",15.0,0.0,30.0,Kind::Choice},
{"Troubleshooting",L"Logging",L"MaxFileMB","Gameplay Log Size Limit (MB)","Maximum size of the gameplay log before it clears and starts over. Higher keeps more recent history but uses more disk space; lower keeps less history. The launcher has a separate fixed limit.",2.0,1.0,16.0,Kind::Slider},
{"Troubleshooting",L"Logging",L"Debug","Detailed Troubleshooting Logs","Include extra technical details in the log to help investigate problems. Leave off for normal play.",0.0,0.0,1.0,Kind::Toggle},
